================================================================================
Vendored quiche (`crates/leyline-quiche/`)
================================================================================

`leyline-quiche` is a fork of Cloudflare's `quiche` (v0.23.7) that links
against `leyline-bssl` instead of upstream `boring`, so Leyline's HTTP/2 and
HTTP/3 ClientHellos share the same patched BoringSSL.

Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/quiche
Copyright: Cloudflare, Inc.
License:   BSD-2-Clause — full text preserved at
           `crates/leyline-quiche/LICENSE` and `crates/leyline-quiche/COPYING`.

Modifications from upstream:
- Package renamed `quiche` -> `leyline-quiche`.
- `boring` / `tokio-boring` dependencies replaced with `leyline-bssl` /
  `leyline-bssl-tokio`.
- Bundled BoringSSL build (`boringssl-vendored` feature) removed — BoringSSL
  is provided by `leyline-bssl-sys` instead.

================================================================================
BoringSSL bindings (vendored under `crates/leyline-bssl*`)
================================================================================

TLS is provided by `leyline-bssl`, `leyline-bssl-sys`, and `leyline-bssl-tokio`,
vendored in-tree as a trimmed fork of Cloudflare's `boring`, `boring-sys`, and
`tokio-boring` crates at tag v5.2.0 (commit
6fdd0a54e81a1eecc76e587c685439d3f2ffdd09), over Google's BoringSSL C library.
`leyline-bssl-sys` builds BoringSSL from source at build time with CMake. The
fork keeps the modules Leyline uses, pins the BoringSSL revision per Chrome era,
and carries these BoringSSL patches:

- `0001-leyline-fingerprint.patch`: `SSL_CTX_set_record_size_limit`
  (RFC 8449), `SSL_CTX_set_delegated_credentials` (RFC 9345),
  `SSL_CTX_set_extension_order`, `SSL_CTX_set_tls13_cipher_order`, the
  ECDHE 3DES cipher suites, and the FFDHE2048/3072 groups. These changes
  first shipped in 0x676e67's `btls` and `boring2` forks
  (https://github.com/0x676e67/btls); Leyline keeps them with that credit.
- `0002-leyline-symbol-prefix.patch`: renames the `ssl_st` and `ssl_session_st`
  C++ structs under the `LEYLINE` symbol prefix.

The `boring` crate derives from Steven Fackler's `rust-openssl`
(https://github.com/sfackler/rust-openssl), and `tokio-boring` derives from
`tokio-openssl` (https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio-openssl). Their copyright
notices are kept in `crates/leyline-bssl/LICENSE`,
`crates/leyline-bssl-tokio/LICENSE-APACHE`, and
`crates/leyline-bssl-tokio/LICENSE-MIT`.

Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/boring
Copyright: Google Inc., Jack Lloyd, Steven Fackler, Ivan Nikulin, and the
           Tokio contributors, as listed in the license files above.
Licenses: the Rust bindings are Apache-2.0 / MIT. The BoringSSL C library is
          Apache-2.0 (relicensed by Google), with a BSD-3-Clause notice for
          Go-derived test tooling that is not linked into the built libraries.

================================================================================
BoringSSL build
================================================================================

`leyline-bssl-sys` ships the BoringSSL source, not binaries. Each build
compiles it from source and links it statically. The full license text
(Apache-2.0 plus the BSD-3-Clause Go notice) is at
`crates/leyline-bssl-sys/LICENSE-BORINGSSL`, and the MIT binding-glue grant at
`crates/leyline-bssl-sys/LICENSE-MIT`.

